                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "456962b4-73b9-30d1-b759-96a3aca97b13",
                        "entry_id": "f38c2a06-6a71-3f8f-b27e-c85c73f4c717",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui date d’après les calculateurs quantiques."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fdf539b4-8314-3fa7-a175-240ce57dd9fb",
                        "entry_id": "f38c2a06-6a71-3f8f-b27e-c85c73f4c717",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui date d’après les calculateurs quantiques.",
                            "[En parlant de cryptographie, notamment] Qui est capable de résister aux assauts d’ordinateurs quantiques."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33b277bb-2d2f-4661-bea6-2ed1dd852cc9",
                                "sense_id": "fdf539b4-8314-3fa7-a175-240ce57dd9fb",
                                "text": "Thales pense également avoir trouvé la parade. Depuis 2013, le groupe travaille sur les algorithmes de cryptologie post-quantique et leur implémentation dans des boîtiers de chiffrement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6545c31a-88cf-4b98-a5f2-41ff0eee188e",
                                "sense_id": "fdf539b4-8314-3fa7-a175-240ce57dd9fb",
                                "text": "L’ANSSI, qui est placée sous l’autorité du Premier ministre, a publié fin 2024 deux études sur le marché français de la cryptographie post-quantique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84fad604-ca8d-4feb-b701-be7f68c6a445",
                        "source_entry_id": "f38c2a06-6a71-3f8f-b27e-c85c73f4c717",
                        "target_lang_word": "post-quantum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "post-quantum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7fc2fc3-9678-34a4-8e28-e545cadd8376",
                                        "entry_id": "85d763bb-a941-3900-b8e0-fd61c0ccd268",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Existing in the hypothetical time period after the development of powerful quantum computers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07f8a51a-6553-493d-bbb1-5b53a7c020c6",
                                                "sense_id": "f7fc2fc3-9678-34a4-8e28-e545cadd8376",
                                                "text": "As research continues on quantum computers, we are quickly approaching the post-quantum age."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81122673-8e5e-4f85-a790-480b4203cdc8",
                                                "sense_id": "f7fc2fc3-9678-34a4-8e28-e545cadd8376",
                                                "text": "Once the need for post-quantum public-key cryptography is established, the question arises what it means for a public-key scheme to be secure in a post-quantum world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32cd1591-a53c-4388-938c-d5e8553da567",
                                                "sense_id": "f7fc2fc3-9678-34a4-8e28-e545cadd8376",
                                                "text": "Computing with Shor’s algorithm is a little further on the horizon than other applications. But adapting to a new post-quantum landscape isn’t just a quick patch download."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8db62de-4800-4362-97ff-ad37c52ec16d",
                                                "sense_id": "f7fc2fc3-9678-34a4-8e28-e545cadd8376",
                                                "text": "The U.S. Department of Commerce’s National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) is stepping in to prepare for this post-quantum future."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "252e06f1-817e-4a5e-b2da-18fba53af104",
                                                "sense_id": "f7fc2fc3-9678-34a4-8e28-e545cadd8376",
                                                "text": "The challenge for post-quantum cryptographers is to encode messages and other data using math problems so complex that even quantum computers can't solve them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14e860c1-759c-3fc4-9f85-246b407e0e71",
                                        "entry_id": "85d763bb-a941-3900-b8e0-fd61c0ccd268",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Existing in the hypothetical time period after the development of powerful quantum computers.",
                                            "Suitable for the post-quantum age; quantum-resistant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c3063db-d874-4e61-9518-061665fdc74d",
                                                "sense_id": "14e860c1-759c-3fc4-9f85-246b407e0e71",
                                                "text": "Cryptographers are at work developing post-quantum algorithms for the future."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12c2cb97-6f42-4beb-80f5-6b96f1a7acc6",
                                                "sense_id": "14e860c1-759c-3fc4-9f85-246b407e0e71",
                                                "text": "There's an entire field of study dedicated to post-quantum cryptography. It's based on writing algorithms that could withstand an attack by a quantum computer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e630abd-52f7-4386-a61d-6268d732e86c",
                                                "sense_id": "14e860c1-759c-3fc4-9f85-246b407e0e71",
                                                "text": "These new algorithms fall into one of two broad categories: quantum and post-quantum."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff95cafb-348c-493a-ae5b-1a4ea9dee8be",
                                                "sense_id": "14e860c1-759c-3fc4-9f85-246b407e0e71",
                                                "text": "Methods such as the RSA algorithm that are used to encrypt things like online transactions are not post-quantum — a large quantum computer could break them, because their security depends on the hardness of factoring large numbers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a52922a2-fb99-4bfe-bb07-a5ee408d9799",
                                                "sense_id": "14e860c1-759c-3fc4-9f85-246b407e0e71",
                                                "text": "The report recommended that companies start working on \"post-quantum decryption\", an emerging field of protecting data in a way that quantum computers could not unlock."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f9dc2e5-00d5-43a7-bd6d-093b1dadddf3",
                                                "sense_id": "14e860c1-759c-3fc4-9f85-246b407e0e71",
                                                "text": "If the data stolen by the balloon was encrypted with post-quantum cybersecurity, it would not be breakable with classical or quantum computers. Therefore, we should upgrade to post-quantum cybersecurity as quickly as possible so that data stolen today remains private for the longest possible time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ee68735-f820-3c35-a4e0-e88b4f4d96be",
                                        "entry_id": "85d763bb-a941-3900-b8e0-fd61c0ccd268",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Beyond quantum physics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1611104e-3610-4941-93f2-1de13461c3b6",
                                                "sense_id": "8ee68735-f820-3c35-a4e0-e88b4f4d96be",
                                                "text": "Marti took us to the Laboratory of Human Evolution, a small library of Mothernalia containing books about quantum and pseudo-quantum and post-quantum science, several copies of Rupert Sheldrake, the nine volumes of the Agenda (Mother's diaries) out on loan, nine tapes of Mother's edited conversations in both French and English."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f22ac45-d00d-4b49-9650-f739341b308b",
                                                "sense_id": "8ee68735-f820-3c35-a4e0-e88b4f4d96be",
                                                "text": "However, before anyone nominates me for a Nobel Prize for solving the mystery of telepathy, I should add that it cannot yet be explained in terms of post-quantum science either."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47b36d2d-164d-43ca-98c3-24accad6e879",
                                                "sense_id": "8ee68735-f820-3c35-a4e0-e88b4f4d96be",
                                                "text": "Even if we do develop a post-quantum explanation of reality, however, we must keep in mind the metaphorical nature of such a model and its limitation as a metaphor for understanding only certain aspects of reality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c8416574-0025-46f6-99bc-dd28657cef87",
                        "source_entry_id": "f38c2a06-6a71-3f8f-b27e-c85c73f4c717",
                        "target_lang_word": "postquantum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "postquantum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04660a62-efc8-3429-840c-65debe94c422",
                                        "entry_id": "612adb3f-780b-31a1-a404-a68c78934459",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of post-quantum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "436b973e-5635-4a91-9f1a-80b1d4704af2",
                                                "sense_id": "04660a62-efc8-3429-840c-65debe94c422",
                                                "text": "And in crossing centuries, languages, and cultural galaxies, factoring in the thousands of elusive elements that come into play, the straightforward algebra of equivalence won't do: if we want to approach it in scientific fashion (as some are wont to), we'll need to look in the direction of postquantum physics, or the nature of scientific study itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1187dab4-66b5-4cf6-b43d-fa5a11a17bc1",
                                                "sense_id": "04660a62-efc8-3429-840c-65debe94c422",
                                                "text": "The administration hopes to cut back on \"systemic\" vulnerabilities at the internet's core, and to adapt to emerging technologies such as postquantum encryption (that is, protection against quantum-based hacks) and digital IDs. Some policies will be largely unchanged."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
